faqs:
  - q: Will your team stay on after launch?
    a: Optional. Most engagements end with a handover to your team, documentation, and a two-week period of embedded support. Continued development can move to a dedicated squad arrangement.
  - q: Do you write tests?
    a: Unit tests for logic, integration tests for critical paths, end-to-end for the happy paths. Coverage reported with every release. The test suite is part of the deliverable.
  - q: What about accessibility?
    a: WCAG 2.1 AA baseline. Audited before launch. Accessibility work is not a separate phase.
  - q: Can you rescue a project that is stuck?
    a: Yes. Rescue engagements start with a 2-week audit, an honest report on what to keep and what to rebuild, and a plan your leadership can sign.
  - q: How do you handle design?
    a: Design and engineering sit in one team. Research and prototyping shape the scope before code starts. Design system baked in so the product does not drift visually after launch.
